  "section_notes": "The final text sets 24-hour incident reporting and a 5% test limit with numeric per-model results shared with regulators and owners but not the public, meeting both companies' confidentiality red lines. The recall trigger is mandatory at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which exposes Halcyon's flagship at 9.9, but stop-sale is left to the regulator. The S3 new-unit shut-off deadline of 36 months falls outside the answer-key acceptable range, so it is the main weakened term."
